{
 "id": "vision_lighting_l1",
 "version": "1.0.0",
 "depends_on": [
  "vision_lighting"
 ],
 "description": "ADVANCED LIGHTING RUNG L1 -- REAL-VALUED ILLUMINANT GAINS. T3 crossed lighting-invariance for the EXACT-RENDERING (integer-ratio) diagonal illuminant class and REFUSED real gains, NAMING the resolution-derived identifiability bound rather than building it. L1 BUILDS it by continuous pose's mechanism transposed from rotation to gain: the illuminant gain is a CONTINUOUS parameter in the CROSS-FRAME MAP (never an in-frame coordinate -- the surfaces' cones stay integers), the held prototype is RENDERED at that continuous gain onto the stepped integer lattice, and recognition is decided by a CONTINUOUS VERDICT (the L-infinity residual) over a proposal from the DISCRETE codebook T3's integer li_mint minted: BINS PROPOSE, CONTINUOUS DECIDES. l1_frame_stats reads the frame's OWN anchor/sum/min/count hub-scoped via Neighbours, into an L1-only attr namespace so T3's arm is readable from the SAME graph; l1_inclass replaces T3's exact order-statistic equality with the ROUNDING ENVELOPE THE LATTICE IMPLIES (a sum clause and a tighter min clause, both necessary, both derived) and mints an IlluminantL1 holding the REAL gain; l1_recognize admits iff the best rendered candidate is within ONE LATTICE STEP; l1_refuse makes a refusal a POSITIVE datum. NO NEW RUST: reuses Div/Times/Minus/Abs/Max/Plus/Lte/MinOver/MaxOver/Argmin/Sum/Count/Neighbours + run_rules. NO MAGIC NUMBER: the bound is ONE LATTICE STEP, falling out as 1/2 (the observation's rounding) + 1/2*(r/a) with r/a <= 1 BY THE DEFINITION OF THE ANCHOR AS THE MAXIMUM -- the analogue of continuous pose's sqrt(2)/2; every envelope term is a half-step rounding scaled by its own cross-multiplier; n is COUNTED from the data. The bound is pinned to OBSERVATIONAL RESOLUTION and to nothing else, so it MUST fail at a dimming gain where distinct materials render onto the same lattice points -- that failure is the measurement. BOUNDED: the GLOBAL diagonal class only. Spatially-varying illuminant / Retinex, global illuminant inference, shadow-vs-reflectance edges and multi-illuminant scenes are NOT solved, only REFUSED; reflectance is GIVEN at the abstract cone-triple grain. Flag-gated on LightingL1Params.lighting_l1, OFF by default (sec 9 -- default 0 => byte-identical, seed inert), read ABSENCE-TOLERANTLY via MaxOver(default 0), never PickUnique. See VISION_LIGHTING_L1_PREREG.md.",
 "microtheory": {
  "id": "vision_lighting_l1_mt",
  "label": "real-valued illuminant gains: the gain as a continuous cross-frame parameter, rendered to the stepped lattice and decided by a continuous verdict pinned to resolution"
 },
