  {
   "name": "l1_frame_stats",
   "comment": "The frame's OWN per-channel order statistics for L1: the ANCHOR l1_a_ch = MaxOver(frame's surfaces, c_ch), the SUM l1_s_ch, the MIN l1_m_ch, and the surface COUNT l1_n. Scoped by Neighbours(frame,'has_surface') -- the frame's own population, NOT a global NodesOfType grab (sec 12.1). Written into an L1-ONLY attribute namespace so NO T3 attribute is ever written by L1: T3's exact arm and L1's continuous arm are then readable from ONE graph in ONE run, which is what makes the CONTINUOUS-DECIDES contrast a measurement rather than two separate experiments. The anchor is the frame's MEASURED dynamic-range ceiling (no constant introduced); the MIN is carried because the min-based in-class clause accumulates only TWO roundings where the sum-based clause accumulates n, giving a tighter falls-out envelope; the COUNT is read from the DATA and is what makes the sum envelope's n a measured quantity rather than a magic number. Matched through a surface edge so the rule only ever sees a frame that HAS a population. The l1_stats_done guard makes it fire once per frame so run_rules converges. Flag-gated, OFF by default (sec 9).",
