  {
   "name": "l1_recognize",
   "comment": "THE REAL-GAIN LIGHTING INVARIANT. A surface in a TEST frame is recognized iff (a) the frame's lighting change was DISCOVERED in-class under the rounding envelope, and (b) the BEST candidate in the reference frame's own held codebook, RENDERED at the continuous cross-frame gain, lies within ONE LATTICE STEP of the observation on every channel. BINS PROPOSE, CONTINUOUS DECIDES: the proposal set is the DISCRETE codebook T3's integer li_mint produced; the decision is the CONTINUOUS rendered residual. The guard is Lte(MinOver(...), LATTICE_STEP) and the effect names the winner with Argmin over the SAME source and the SAME value -- continuous pose's cp_recognize shape exactly, which is the precedent that an Argmin (unlike a Pick(Filter(...))) does apply its value expression in effect position. MinOver carries an explicit NO_CANDIDATE default so an EMPTY codebook REFUSES rather than silently admitting (an absent population must never read as a match, sec 1.1). THE BOUND IS NOT TUNED: 1.0 is ONE STEP OF THE INTEGER LATTICE, derived as 1/2 (the observation's own rounding) + 1/2*(r/a) with r/a <= 1 BY THE DEFINITION OF THE ANCHOR AS THE FRAME'S MAXIMUM -- the analogue of continuous pose's sqrt(2)/2 half-diagonal. It is therefore pinned to OBSERVATIONAL RESOLUTION and to nothing else, and it MUST fail when the resolution is inadequate: at a dimming gain distinct materials render onto the same lattice points and no verdict can separate what the steps did not record. That failure is the measurement, not a defect. Flag-gated, OFF by default (sec 9).",
